    <help sid="HelpGarageAndDealersLineOfBusiness_Question_KASCode_A">
      <value>Enter Y for a &#x201C;Yes&#x201D; response. Input N for &#x201C;No&#x201D; response. Indicates the response to the question, &#x201C;Any drivers with convictions for moving traffic violations?&#x201D;.
Applicable only in Kansas: Under Kansas law, the following traffic violations are not required to be reported to insurers:
1. A speeding violation of up to six (6) mph that occurs in an area with a maximum posted speed limit from 30 mph through 54 mph, or
2. A speeding violation of up to ten (10) mph that occurs in an area with a maximum posted speed limit from 55 mph through 75 mph. </value>
    </help>
